    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthAccountHint">This account signs in through your browser. If it stops connecting, use the button below to sign in again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthErrorBlocked">Google blocked this sign-in. In Google Cloud Console, open 'OAuth consent screen' and add this account's email to 'Test users' - the app is unverified and uses Gmail's restricted scope, so only test users can sign in, and refresh tokens expire after 7 days.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthErrorInvalidClient">The client ID or secret does not match. Recreate the credentials in Google Cloud Console as a 'Desktop app' client and paste the new client ID in File &gt; Options.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthErrorMismatch">This usually means the OAuth client was created as a 'Web application'. Create it again as a 'Desktop app' in Google Cloud Console - desktop clients accept any port on http://127.0.0.1 without registering a redirect URI.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthHeader">Sign-in (OAuth2)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthHintBrowser">Your browser will open so you can sign in. Imvello never sees your password.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthHintNeedClientId">Browser sign-in needs a {0} OAuth client ID. Add it in File &gt; Options first</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthHintParagraph">Optional. To use 'Sign in with Google / Microsoft', register a Desktop-app OAuth client in Google Cloud Console or Microsoft Entra (Azure) and paste its client ID here. For Google: choose 'Desktop app' (Google accepts any loopback port, nothing to register as redirect URI) and add your email under 'Test users' on the OAuth consent screen - the Gmail mail scope requires it while the app is unverified. Gmail also works with an App Password, without a client ID.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthHintUseAppPassword">, or use an App Password below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.OAuthSignInTimedOut">Sign-in was not completed. If an error page appeared in the browser: use a 'Desktop app' OAuth client and add your address as a test user on the OAuth consent screen (File &gt; Options).</sys:String>
