    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.GmailStepsTitle" xml:space="preserve">Connect Gmail in 3 steps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.GmailSteps" xml:space="preserve">1. Click "Create App Password" below and sign in to Google (2-Step Verification must be on).&#x0a;2. Type Imvello as the app name and click Create.&#x0a;3. Copy the 16-letter password, paste it below and click Connect.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.GoogleClientIdInvalid" xml:space="preserve">The Google client ID is not valid. It must look like 123456789012-abc123def456.apps.googleusercontent.com.&#x0a;&#x0a;In Google Cloud Console &gt; APIs &amp; Services &gt; Credentials, copy the "Client ID" of a "Desktop app" OAuth client - not the project ID or the client secret. You can also paste the whole downloaded JSON file into the Client ID box.&#x0a;&#x0a;Or leave it empty and connect Gmail with an App Password, which needs no setup.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.GoogleClientSecretMissing" xml:space="preserve">Google browser sign-in also needs the client secret. Paste it in File &gt; Options &gt; Google client secret, or connect with an App Password instead.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.MicrosoftClientIdInvalid" xml:space="preserve">The Microsoft client ID is not valid. It must be the "Application (client) ID" GUID, like 1a2b3c4d-1234-5678-9abc-1234567890ab.&#x0a;&#x0a;In the Azure Portal &gt; App registrations, open your app and copy "Application (client) ID" from the Overview page - not the tenant ID, object ID or a client secret.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Dialogs.MicrosoftOAuthErrorClient" xml:space="preserve">Fix the app registration in the Azure Portal (App registrations):&#x0a;1. Authentication &gt; Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft accounts".&#x0a;2. Authentication &gt; Add a platform &gt; "Mobile and desktop applications" &gt; custom redirect URI: http://localhost&#x0a;3. API permissions &gt; Add &gt; APIs my organization uses &gt; "Office 365 Exchange Online" &gt; Delegated: IMAP.AccessAsUser.All and SMTP.Send.&#x0a;Then copy the "Application (client) ID" into File &gt; Options.</sys:String>
